Exp 1b:Binary Search

Aim:
To write a Java program to search for an element in an array using the binary search method.

Algorithm:
1. Start the program.
2. Read the array elements and the key to be searched.
3. Initialize low = 0 and high = n - 1.
4. Find the middle element using mid = (low + high) / 2.
5. If the middle element equals the key, display the position.
6. If the key is smaller, search the left half; otherwise, search the right half.
7. Repeat until the element is found or the search range becomes empty.
8. Stop the program.

Program:
import java.util.Scanner;
public class BinarySearch {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        int a[] = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};
        int low = 0, high = a.length - 1;
        int mid, key, found = 0;

        System.out.print("Enter element to search: ");
        key = sc.nextInt();

        while (low <= high) {
            mid = (low + high) / 2;

            if (a[mid] == key) {
                System.out.println("Element found at position " + (mid + 1));
                found = 1;
                break;
            } else if (key < a[mid]) {
                high = mid - 1;
            } else {
                low = mid + 1;
            }
        }

        if (found == 0) {
            System.out.println("Element not found");
        }

        sc.close();
    }
}

